  "title": "2026-07-25-eval-160035 · rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "description": "# RAG ingestion, retrieval, and lifecycle\n\nA left-to-right ingestion flow carries source content and ACLs through normalization, version classification, chunking, embedding, and version-consistent publication. Failure branches isolate parse errors and exhausted retries without stopping healthy work. The query lane rewrites searches, combines vector and keyword retrieval, reranks and applies user permissions, then either returns a cited grounded answer or declines when evidence is weak. A separate generation-rebuild lane supports atomic promotion and rollback, while feedback turns unanswered or weakly served questions into ingestion priorities.",
  "mode": "diagram",
